  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the two files required for this task:\n\n1. **`lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py`** \u2014 contains the root cause: `_extract_tar_dir()` looks up directory members via a custom `tar._ansible_normalized_cache` dict (built in `install_artifact()`) instead of the standard `tarfile.getmember()` API. The cache strips trailing path separators from names, which mismatches archives that store directory entries under their canonical (non-suffixed) name \u2014 this is the CPython tarfile workaround referenced in the bug report.\n\n2. **`test/units/cli/galaxy/test_collection_extract_tar.py`** \u2014 the existing unit test file for `_extract_tar_dir`, showing the established mocking pattern (mocking `tar._ansible_normalized_cache` directly, using `mocker`, asserting `AnsibleError` on lookup failure). This is essential context for writing a regression test that fits the codebase's existing test conventions and exercises the same function.",
